kind how-do-i
title How do I try a whole look on the console before I install it?
intro The live trial shows a look on the console for a few seconds: its font set, its size and its color scheme. A size can only be tried when the console lets programs resize its grid.
see looks/make-a-look-and-use-it-on-the-console
waits-for CF1 item 2: the live trial carries only the font set's name

# The console lets programs resize its grid, which is how vtium-config
# tries a size.
file etc/vtium.conf
    version = 1
    font-name = unifont
    allow-window-ops = on
    [head console]
    vt = 5
file etc/batch.conf
    ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
font fonts/mono.bdf 8x16
frit mono
    source=bdf:ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf

1. Go to the Looks tab.
2. Choose New look.
3. Erase the name.
4. Type big.
5. Press Enter.
6. Set Font set to mono.
7. Choose Size.
8. Choose 24 pt.
9. Set Color scheme to vga.
10. Press Esc.
11. Press t to try live.
note The console shows mono at 24 pt, 32 pixels high, in the color scheme vga.
at the trial
check console received "\e]50;mono"
check console draws mono
check console palette vga
check console grid 50x15

12. Press Esc.
note Any key but k puts the console back as it was.
at the end of the trial
check console draws unifont
check console palette legacy
check console grid 100x30
